<title>GERMANY: E.German Nov industry output falls 0.3 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>E.German Nov industry output falls 0.3 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT    Nov 96     Oct 96	Nov 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)  -0.3	 -1.4	  +3.9</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +0.1	 +4.3	   n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)	     140.2	140.6	 140.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbnk statistics. Previously reported data in brackets.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				     Nov 96	     Oct 96</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Manufacturing output   154.0	+1.0     152.5	 -3.7</p>
<p>Including:</p>
<p>  Intermediate goods    185.7	+0.9     184.0	 -0.2</p>
<p>  Capital goods	   130.6	+4.3     125.2	 -4.2</p>
<p> Energy output	     82.8	-3.3	85.6	 -1.3</p>
<p> Construction	     203.8	-0.9     205.7	 +3.7</p>
<p>Two month comparison Oct/Nov 96 with Aug/Sept 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output			 -2.5</p>
<p>Two month comparison Oct/Nov 96 with Oct/Nov 95:</p>
<p> Industrial output			 +1.6</p>
<p> Mining				     -15.6</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		   +5.8</p>
<p>  Including:Intermediate goods	 +6.8</p>
<p>		Capital goods		+5.1</p>
<p>		Consumer durables	 -10.5</p>
<p>		Consumer goods	     +7.7</p>
<p> Energy output			     -3.1</p>
<p> Construction				-1.9</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49-28-26097150</p>
</text>
